@page "/guides/getting-started"

<PageTitle>Getting started · Trailblazor</PageTitle>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Headline" As="TextElement.H1">Getting started</TbText>
<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle" class="docs-lead">
    Add Trailblazor to a Blazor app for .NET 10, render your first component, and choose a render mode.
</TbText>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">1. Add the library</TbText>
<TbText>
    Trailblazor isn't on NuGet yet. Until it is, clone the repository and reference the library from your app's
    project file.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="Project reference" Code="@ProjectReference" />

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">2. Register the services</TbText>
<TbText>
    In <code>Program.cs</code>, register the services the components use: dialogs, toasts and screen-reader
    announcements.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="Program.cs" Code="@Services" />

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">3. Import the namespace</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="_Imports.razor" Code="@Imports" />

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">4. Add TbRoot to the layout</TbText>
<TbText>
    Put one <code>&lt;TbRoot /&gt;</code> in the main layout. It adds Trailblazor's stylesheet to the page head and
    hosts the dialogs, toasts and announcements that services open from code.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="MainLayout.razor" Code="@Layout" />
<TbText>
    The dialogs and toasts a page opens show only when <code>TbRoot</code> hosts them in the same interactive session
    as that page. When the whole app is interactive, with the same render mode on <code>Routes</code> and
    <code>HeadOutlet</code>, it already does.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="App.razor" Code="@App" />
<TbText>
    When interactivity is set page by page, as in the default Blazor template, the layout renders statically. Give
    <code>TbRoot</code> the render mode your interactive pages use, and it hosts dialogs, toasts and announcements in
    that mode while the stylesheet stays in the static page head. Every page then starts an interactive session for
    these hosts, even a fully static one, and only pages in that same render mode can open them.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="MainLayout.razor, interactivity per page" Code="@PerPageLayout" />

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">5. Use a component</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="A first component" Code="@FirstComponent" />

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Render modes</TbText>
<TbText>
    Every component works in Interactive Server, Interactive WebAssembly and Interactive Auto. Pages rendered as static
    server-side rendering still show every component; fields post their values with a form, and a select renders the
    browser's own <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>. Anything that responds to clicks or keys, such as a dialog, a menu or
    tabs, needs an interactive render mode.
</TbText>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">App-wide options</TbText>
<TbText>
    <code>AddTrailblazor</code> takes the settings that apply to every dialog and toast. A dialog's own options still
    override them.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="App-wide options" Code="@Options" />

@code {
    private const string ProjectReference = """
        <ItemGroup>
          <ProjectReference Include="..\trailblazor\src\Trailblazor\Trailblazor.csproj" />
        </ItemGroup>
        """;

    private const string Services = """
        builder.Services.AddTrailblazor();
        """;

    private const string App = """
        <head>
            ...
            <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
        </head>
        <body>
            <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
            <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
        </body>
        """;

    private const string Imports = """
        @using Trailblazor
        """;

    private const string Layout = """
        @inherits LayoutComponentBase

        <TbRoot />

        <main>
            @Body
        </main>
        """;

    private const string PerPageLayout = """
        @inherits LayoutComponentBase

        <TbRoot HostRenderMode="InteractiveServer" />

        <main>
            @Body
        </main>
        """;

    private const string FirstComponent = """
        <TbButton OnClick="SaveAsync">Save</TbButton>

        @code {
            private Task SaveAsync() => Task.CompletedTask;
        }
        """;

    private const string Options = """
        using Trailblazor;

        builder.Services.AddTrailblazor(options =>
        {
            options.Dialogs.DismissOnBackdrop = false;
            options.Toasts.Position = ToastPosition.BottomEnd;
        });
        """;
}
